# The row version variation point attaches to the PostgreSQL example: it adds
# the CompleteItem command with its scenarios, the shared scenarios of the
# version over a table of notes, the INeverChanges mark, and the migration EF
# Core writes for the row version (no DDL in the SQL: xmin is a system column),
# and changes only the application over a table that changes - its entity, its
# commands, its CLI resource and output. No file of the store's mechanism
# changes: EF Core compares a row version an entity declares.
base library/architecture/dotnet/vp-postgres-in-dotnet.skill/examples
# the entity carries its version; the configuration and the model snapshot follow it
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Domain/Entities/Item.cs
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Domain/Configurations/ItemConfiguration.cs
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Domain/Todo.Domain.csproj
change src/Infrastructure/Postgres/Postgres/Migrations/AppDbContextModelSnapshot.cs
# the module's errors: a change with no version, an item that is not there
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Domain/Errors/TodoErrors.cs
# the answers carry the id and the version; the item for a change is read untracked
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Commands/PlanItemsCommand.cs
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application/Commands/AddItemHandler.cs
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application/Commands/ListItemsHandler.cs
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application/Specifications/ItemsOfList.cs
# The CLI adds CompleteItem; persistent items carry ids and opaque versions.
change src/App/App.Host/Api/Cli/Endpoint/ListsHandler.cs
change src/App/App.Host.Tests/Steps/Cli/CliListsSteps.cs
change src/App/App.Host.Tests/features/Cli/lists-in-dotnet.feature
# the scenarios of the changed answers and of the whole application over its database
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application.Tests/Commands/Steps/ItemListsSteps.cs
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application.Tests/Commands/features/item-lists-in-dotnet.feature
change src/App/App.Host.Tests/Steps/PersistenceSteps.cs
change README.md
